Generate a fresh pre-auth key at https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys
and place it (just the key, nothing else) at /etc/tailscale/authkey on the
router, mode 0600. Do not reuse the key that was in the live OPNsense
config - Tailscale pre-auth keys are typically single-use and it's almost
certainly already consumed by the existing node.

If you'd rather log in interactively instead of using a key, just delete
/etc/tailscale/authkey (or never create it) and run `tailscale up
--advertise-routes=10.0.0.0/24 --advertise-exit-node --accept-routes` by
hand once after boot; the tailscale-autoconnect.service unit skips itself
once the node is already logged in.
